{
  "The commands around tabs: context menus on tabs and on the empty strip, a searchable list of a group's documents, application toolbar buttons, the recently used list, back and forward, reopening closed documents, locked groups, and keyboard shortcuts for all of them.": "",
  "Context menus": "",
  "Each tab offers the commands for its document, and the empty strip offers the commands for its group. `menuItems` hides built-in items, and `onContextMenuOpening` changes the list for each document or cancels it. `newDocument` creates a document when the empty strip is double-clicked.": "",
  "Command": "",
  "Item": "",
  "Note": "",
  "Close": "",
  "Closes the tab. Its key is shown next to it.": "",
  "Close others / to the right / to the left / saved / all": "",
  "Pinned tabs stay while `keepPinned` is on.": "",
  "Copy the title": "",
  "Copies it to the clipboard.": "",
  "Keep open": "",
  "Available only on a preview tab.": "",
  "Pin / Unpin": "",
  "Shows whichever applies.": "",
  "Split up / down / left / right": "",
  "Creates a new group on that side with the document, or a copy (see `splitCopies`).": "",
  "Move to the next / previous group": "",
  "Splits if no group exists in that direction.": "",
  "Move to…": "",
  "Chooses the destination with the keyboard ([Drag and drop](/tabdocs/drag#keys)).": "",
  "Move group to… (empty strip)": "",
  "The same for the whole group.": "",
  "New document (empty strip)": "",
  "Available only with `newDocument`.": "",
  "Reopen closed (empty strip)": "",
  "Disabled when nothing can be reopened.": "",
  "Lock group / Unlock group (empty strip)": "",
  "The open documents list and toolbar buttons": "",
  "The “…” button (or Ctrl+K Ctrl+P) lists the group's documents, or the documents of every group with `openListScope: 'all'`. Type to search, and press Enter to open. `toolbarItems` adds application buttons to every group, and a document's `actions` appear while it is active.": "",
  "Recently used, back and forward, and reopen": "",
  "The recently used list switches between documents in the same way as Ctrl+Tab in code editors. `goBack` and `goForward` follow the documents activated in every group, and `reopenClosed` opens the most recently closed document in its original place.": "",
  "Locked groups": "",
  "`lock(group)` reserves a group for its current contents. `open` without a group uses another group, or a new group beside it when all are locked (a single group still accepts it). The lock is saved with the layout.": "",
  "A page in a browser tab never receives Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+T, Ctrl+Page Up/Down and often Ctrl+1…9, because the browser reserves them. A manager therefore starts with keys that reach it, in the same way as the web version of a code editor (Ctrl+Alt in place of a reserved Ctrl, and Ctrl+E, the Quick Open key, for the recent list), and keeps the desktop key as a second option. An installed app (standalone display mode) receives every key, and there `keyPreset: 'auto'` uses `TabDocumentManager.desktopKeys`. `keys` changes any of them, and an empty list disables one.": "",
  "Browser tab": "",
  "Installed app": "",
  "Ctrl + W, Ctrl + F4": "",
  "Ctrl + Page Down / Page Up": "",
  "Moves to the next or previous tab (`nextTab`, `previousTab`).": "",
  "Ctrl + 1 … 9": "",
  "Sets focus on a group (`focusGroup`).": "",
  "Ctrl + Tab, Ctrl + Shift + Tab": "",
  "Opens the recently used list and moves through it while Ctrl is held. Releasing Ctrl opens the highlighted document (`recentNext`, `recentPrevious`).": "",
  "Moves back and forward (`goBack`, `goForward`).": "",
  "Ctrl + Shift + T": "",
  "Reopens the most recently closed document (`reopenClosed`).": "",
  "Closes the group's documents, or its saved documents (`closeAllTabs`, `closeSavedTabs`).": "",
  "Keeps a preview tab open (`keepOpen`).": "",
  "Pins or unpins the active document (`togglePin`).": "",
  "Opens the \"…\" list (`showOpenList`).": "",
  "Splits to the right (`splitRight`).": "",
  "Opens the context menu of the focused tab.": "",
  "The kit's `ContextMenu`: a `menu` opened by a right-click, Shift+F10 or the Menu key on a tab, and named after the document (or after the group, on the strip). Focus returns to the tab when it closes.": "",
  "A single menu with a search field, the documents as a `menu` named “Open documents” (`menuitemradio` items with the displayed document checked, and each announcing its description, group and unsaved changes), and a `menu` of commands. Up and Down move from the search through the documents and commands, typing on a document returns to the search, Tab moves between parts, Enter opens, and Escape closes.": "",
  "The same document menu, named “Recently used documents”, with focus on the highlighted document so that it is announced as it moves. It also works without holding a key: the arrow keys move, a letter jumps to a title, Enter opens, and Escape closes.": "",
  "A locked group is named “Group 1, locked”, and its toolbar has an “Unlock group” button.": "",
  "Locked and unlocked are announced politely, like the other changes.": "",
  "The context menus of tabs and of the empty strip.": "",
  "`false` hides a built-in item: `{ copyTitle: false }`.": "",
  "The \"…\" button in each group's toolbar.": "",
  "Whether the \"…\" list and the recently used list show the group's documents or those of every group.": "",
  "Application buttons in every group's toolbar, created once per group (text, `icon`, `hint`, `tone`, `visible`, `enabled`, `click` …).": "",
  "Creates a new document when the empty strip is double-clicked, and for the strip menu.": "",
  "The number of activated documents `goBack` remembers. 0 disables the history.": "",
  "The number of closed documents `reopenClosed` remembers. 0 disables it. Only documents whose content can be recreated (a `content` function, the `factory` or a copy) are kept.": "",
  "The default keys (see Keyboard). `auto` uses the desktop keys when the page runs as an installed app.": "",
  "The split, maximize and \"…\" buttons.": "",
  "Buttons in the group's toolbar while this document is active, placed before the built-in buttons.": "",
  "Opens a group's \"…\" list, to search and open documents, close all, close saved, and lock or unlock.": "",
  "Opens the recently used list, with the next document (or the last, with `-1`) highlighted.": "",
  "Activates the previous or next document in the history, in any group. `canGoBack` and `canGoForward` indicate whether one exists (reactive).": "",
  "Reopens the most recently closed document, in its original group and position. `closedDocuments` lists them (reactive).": "",
  "Also available as `group.lock()` and `group.unlock()`. `group.locked` reads the state.": "",
  "Creates a document with `newDocument` and opens it.": "",
  "`'next'`, `'previous'`, or the group on a side (`'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'`, `'down'`). Splits if no group exists in that direction.": "",
  "Writes the title to the clipboard.": "",
  "The open documents of every group, most recently activated first.": "",
  "`{ document, group, items, byKeyboard }`, cancelable. `document` is `null` for the empty strip. Change `items` (each built-in item has its command in `data`) or add your own.": "",
  "`{ group, byUser }`. The `…ing` events are cancelable.": "",
  "See the [overview](/tabdocs#api) for the rest of the API, and [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs) for preview and pinned tabs, sizes and copies.": ""
}
